        "id": 1137668
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-08-24T22:41:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hmm it looks like after the compression completes, if the compressed value is larger than the original input, then it rereads the file and copies it into the zip under the method Stored. That requires us to either preemptively keep a copy of the file (which seems wasteful to me), or requires a way to go back and reread the file later.\n\nIt does seem cleaner to me if the reader were to provide a Clone function instead of a Seek function, and a cloned readers would lazily reread the file from its own position, so there\u0027s less state shared between reads.\n\nWould you like something like that instead?",
      "parentUuid": "f1bdc91e_4b90caf2",
      "revId": "f765ef7965092e3b3708185f3b8bd4a6c0ffa495",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
